a-1f6d190b8132\",\"_type\":\"ngsmain-quoteBlock\",\"colorTheme\":\"white-background-with-yellow-quote\",\"entity\":null,\"headerPreset\":null,\"headingsDecorator\":\"off\",\"label\":\"Our Promise\",\"quotesList\":[{\"_id\":\"6a73763d-14b5-4487-99d1-bb72939ebeef\",\"_type\":\"ngsmain-quote\",\"anchorId\":null,\"layoutVariation\":{\"imagePosition\":\"image-right\",\"imageToggle\":true,\"mediaAsset\":{\"_key\":\"QoZTMRn3pJmxJRg88aD0l\",\"_type\":\"cloudinary.asset\",\"_version\":1,\"access_control\":[],\"access_mode\":\"public\",\"bytes\":30029693,\"created_at\":\"2026-04-30T18:49:03Z\",\"created_by\":{\"id\":\"fcf45803a4ef12e6d96a234cd1a15d\",\"type\":\"user\"},\"folder\":\"NGS Main Site/Home\",\"folder_id\":\"cb0a7a8cad060d49e7e29e383442cf43f6\",\"format\":\"jpg\",\"height\":5504,\"id\":\"da699fff09f8815da562fa7331719255\",\"metadata\":{},\"public_id\":\"NGS Main Site/Home/02_NS119048977_2023EXPLR_Karanth_cr_Alisha_Vasudev_1129_1364\",\"resource_type\":\"image\",\"secure_url\":\"https://images.nationalgeographic.org/image/upload/v1777574943/NGS%20Main%20Site/Home/02_NS119048977_2023EXPLR_Karanth_cr_Alisha_Vasudev_1129_1364.jpg\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"upload\",\"uploaded_by\":{\"id\":\"fcf45803a4ef12e6d96a234cd1a15d\",\"type\":\"user\"},\"url\":\"http://images.nationalgeographic.org/image/upload/v1777574943/NGS%20Main%20Site/Home/02_NS119048977_2023EXPLR_Karanth_cr_Alisha_Vasudev_1129_1364.jpg\",\"version\":1777574943,\"width\":8256}},\"location\":null,\"personsName\":\"Krithi K. Karanth\",\"quotedWords\":[{\"_key\":\"be862ecf136e\",\"_type\":\"block\",\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"8438d5a9ab97\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"“This recognition provides a distinguished global platform to elevate our innovative, impactful and scalable conservation programs while fostering empathy, deepening impact and promoting a collective stewardship of the natural world.”\"}],\"markDefs\":[],\"style\":\"normal\"}],\"roleOrJobTitle\":\"2026 Rolex National Geographic Explorer of the Year\",\"url\":null,\"urlLabel\":null}],\"statement\":null,\"subtitle\":null,\"title\":\"Supporting Conservation for the 21st Century\",\"url\":{\"label\":null,\"link\":null}}]}]\n24:[\"$\",\"section\",\"8d4a05f3-83ad-4f04-b38a-3243bc71e3c2\",{\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L2c\",null,{\"_id\":\"8d4a05f3-83ad-4f04-b38a-3243bc71e3c2\",\"_type\":\"ngsmain-teaseBlock\",\"backgroundVariation\":\"light\",\"entity\":null,\"headerPreset\":null,\"label\":\"Our Funding Strategy\",\"overview\":null,\"statement\":null,\"teasesList\":[{\"_id\":\"6a413add-534e-4296-8b03-7a302064a5f4\",\"_type\":\"ngsmain-tease\",\"anchorId\":null,\"ctaButtons\":[{\"_type\":\"ngsmain-ctaButton\",\"text\":\"See Opportunities\",\"url\":\"https://www.nationalgeographic.org/explore/grants-investments\",\"variation\":\"Primary\"}],\"description\":null,\"label\":null,\"media\":{\"_key\":\"ho0LjZox6sqQz2zNZf4zk\",\"_type\":\"cloudinary.asset\",\"_version\":1,\"access_control\":[],\"access_mode\":\"public\",\"bytes\":3930226,\"context\":{\"custom\":{\"alt\":\"Photo by Jason Gulley. The Rodman Reservoir was created in 1968 by building the Kirkpatrick Dam across the Oklawaha River as part of a cross-Florida canal system that was never completed. The reservoir flooded at least 20 springs and the dam which created it blocks access to most manatees and several species of fish that historically migrated seasonally into the spring-fed Silver River. Removing the dam would restore access to the species but the reservoir has become a popular fishing and boatin\",\"caption\":\"Photo by Jason Gulley. The Rodman Reservoir was created in 1968 by building the Kirkpatrick Dam across the Oklawaha River as part of a cross-Florida canal syste\"}},\"created_at\":\"2025-04-08T11:10:58Z\",\"created_by\":{\"id\":\"759212413777513\",\"type\":\"accesskey\"},\"folder\":\"NGS Main Site/Grants and Investments\",\"folder_id\":\"cb0a8c096c8612716f62c3af4389e642cc\",\"format\":\"jpg\",\"height\":3800,\"id\":\"65c8683528271aa2ed08dbb70f57faca\",\"metadata\":{\"credits\":\"Jason Gulley\",\"short_description\":\"Photo by Jason Gulley. The Rodman Reservoir was created in 1968 by building the Kirkpatrick Dam across the Oklawaha River as part of a cross-Florida canal system that was never completed. The reservoir flooded at least 20 springs and the dam which created it blocks access to most manatees and several species of fish that historically migrated seasonally into the spring-fed Silver River. Removing the dam would restore access to the species but the reservoir has become a popular fishing and boating destination. Photographed from an R44 helicopter piloted by Parker Thornley.\"},\"public_id\":\"NGS Main Site/Grants and Investments/2024-10-NS119765196_NGS-98110S-23_MediaAssetSubmission_23_\",\"resource_type\":\"image\",\"secure_url\":\"https://images.nationalgeographic.org/image/upload/v1744110658/NGS%20Main%20Site/Grants%20and%20Investments/2024-10-NS119765196_NGS-98110S-23_MediaAssetSubmission_23_.jpg\",\"tags\":[\"Grants and Investments\"],\"type\":\"upload\",\"uploaded_by\":{\"id\":\"759212413777513\",\"type\":\"accesskey\"},\"url\":\"http://images.nationalgeographic.org/image/upload/v1744110658/NGS%20Main%20Site/Grants%20and%20Investments/2024-10-NS119765196_NGS-98110S-23_MediaAssetSubmission_23_.jpg\",\"version\":1744110658,\"width\":5700},\"mediaVariation\":\"fill\",\"subtitle\":\"We fund individuals working on projects in science, conservation, storytelling, education and technology that align with one or more of our focus areas.\",\"title\":\"Grant Opportunities\"}],\"title\":\"Supporting Explorers and Changemakers\",\"url\":{\"label\":null,\"link\":null}}]}]\n25:[\"$\",\"section\",\"2c63370c-e8d9-4141-8f1b-1b99ba1e21e0\",{\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L2d\",null,{\"_id\":\"2c63370c-e8d9-4141-8f1b-1b99ba1e21e0\",\"_type\":\"ngsmain-newsUpdatesBlock\",\"articles\":[{\"_id\":\"0d37fcf8-543f-4945-8bad-85019ecd9393\",\"_type\":\"news_article\",\"anchorId